    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="318ed351-a859-58bc-b312-8a03cdbe70c7" activityNameId="f72260f5-b245-5b03-a427-c1602afe57fb" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, biogas from maize silage, at cogen</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, biogas from maize silage, at cogen
The multioutput process "biogas gas burned in cogen with gas engine" delivers the co-products: heat and electricity. The allocation is based on the exergy values of heat and electricity. The exergy value of electricity is 1, and the exergy value of heat is 0.17.  The degrees of efficiency are as follows: electricity: 0.354 and heat: 0.51.;
UUID: cd6b5050-fb37-34ab-9d16-e129bdaf6aeb
Use of biogas in a cogeneration unit. Included are emissions to air, biogas consumption, use and disposal of operational supplements as well as infrastructure expenditures.
Location: Conditions of cogeneration in Switzerland.
Technology: Lambda 1-engine" with a catalytic converter
Time period: undefined
Production volume: In 2002 the production of electricity from biogas was 9.8 GWh/a.
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cd6b5050-fb37-34ab-9d16-e129bdaf6aeb.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
